Example programs the compiler accepts with warnings, one case per
program, in byte order of name.

Each case is a txtar file pair: <name>/main.tck holds the program and
<name>/expected the warnings the compiler gives it, with the program's
path printed as <name>/main.tck. An empty <name>/no-final-newline file
after the pair means the program's last line has no newline. The format
is invalid.txtar's, which internal/invalid documents; go test ./test -run
TestWarnings checks that every case compiles with exactly its warnings,
and -update rewrites the expected sections.

-- any-switch-unused-binding/main.tck --
package main

func f(a any) int64 {
    switch v := a.(type) {
    case int64:
        return 1
    default:
        return 0
    }
}

func main() {
}
